(4656018, 667791, 22970, '<td valign="top">I like your photograph. But I will say this. You have to look at it for at least 5 seconds for the bids face to become clear. For some reason it''s blends together when you first open the picture but as the seconds go by it becomes clear. That to me is the only issue I see with the picture. Maybe voters didn''t give the picture time, resulting in a lower vote. I did not get to vote but I would of given it a 6 possibly a 7 because of the composition and nice broken background. The focus is great and I really like the detail in the wood grain.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I like your photograph. But I will say this. You have to look at it for at least 5 seconds for the bids face to become clear. For some reason it''s blends together when you first open the picture but as the seconds go by it becomes clear. That to me is the only issue I see with the picture. Maybe voters didn''t give the picture time, resulting in a lower vote. I did not get to vote but I would of given it a 6 possibly a 7 because of the composition and nice broken background. The focus is great and I really like the detail in the wood grain. ', '2008-04-23 17:39:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656029, 667791, 83845, '<td valign="top">The wood grain is awesome, but the bright lower right hand corner draws my eyes away from everything.  A little off each side, maybe?... making it a vertical photo?</td>', 'The wood grain is awesome, but the bright lower right hand corner draws my eyes away from everything.  A little off each side, maybe?... making it a vertical photo?', '2008-04-23 17:47:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656032, 667791, 73942, '<td valign="top">I''m somewhat new to this but since you''ve asked for comments, I''ll give it a try.  There is great detail in the wood and I think in this challenge, people voted high for detail.  The DOF is done well. All I can see that is missing is color.  Maybe a little more color would have made it more interesting and therefore may have scored higher, especially with the speed voters.</td>', 'I''m somewhat new to this but since you''ve asked for comments, I''ll give it a try.  There is great detail in the wood and I think in this challenge, people voted high for detail.  The DOF is done well. All I can see that is missing is color.  Maybe a little more color would have made it more interesting and therefore may have scored higher, especially with the speed voters.', '2008-04-23 17:48:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656045, 667791, 27617, '<td valign="top">I like the use of bokeh and like was said before the wood grain is really neat. However, because the wood is soooooo sharp and defined by the white lines it draws the focus away from the bird because of his face being in his chest. Composition wise I would have lowered the fence from dead center to follow the rule of thirds line but its still nice the way it is. I''m sure this looks great positive but alas that would have been DNMC lol good work!</td>', 'I like the use of bokeh and like was said before the wood grain is really neat. However, because the wood is soooooo sharp and defined by the white lines it draws the focus away from the bird because of his face being in his chest. Composition wise I would have lowered the fence from dead center to follow the rule of thirds line but its still nice the way it is. I''m sure this looks great positive but alas that would have been DNMC lol good work!', '2008-04-23 18:00:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656068, 669990, 34938, '<td valign="top">Hi Naomi...I have been away a few days in Brisbane, and I just got home and saw this...how sensational! How well deserved! Congratulations...See you at the next DPC Connect group! You''ll have to tell us all about it...Enzo</td>', 'Hi Naomi...I have been away a few days in Brisbane, and I just got home and saw this...how sensational! How well deserved! Congratulations...See you at the next DPC Connect group! You''ll have to tell us all about it...Enzo', '2008-04-23 18:18:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656070, 667791, 54645, '<td valign="top">Nice image, better than mine which recieved zero comments as well during the challenge! I agree that at first glance, I''m drawn to the texture of the fence. If this was advanced editing, I think an curves adjustment layer(choose color negative) of the image after it was inverted would help bring out the eye (would need a mask of course...advanced editing rules I believe). Don''t know for sure without trying. I gave this shot a 6 during voting.</td>', 'Nice image, better than mine which recieved zero comments as well during the challenge! I agree that at first glance, I''m drawn to the texture of the fence. If this was advanced editing, I think an curves adjustment layer(choose color negative) of the image after it was inverted would help bring out the eye (would need a mask of course...advanced editing rules I believe). Don''t know for sure without trying. I gave this shot a 6 during voting.', '2008-04-23 18:19:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656071, 667745, 34938, '<td valign="top">You are well ahead of the game my friend...congrats on another great image and ribbon...Enzo</td>', 'You are well ahead of the game my friend...congrats on another great image and ribbon...Enzo', '2008-04-23 18:19:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656074, 669967, 37252, '<td valign="top">I think what kept your image from scoring higher was that the bee gets lost in the business of the image. I would have cropped off the flowers on the extreme left, right up to the next row. The colors are details were all executed well.</td>', 'I think what kept your image from scoring higher was that the bee gets lost in the business of the image. I would have cropped off the flowers on the extreme left, right up to the next row. The colors are details were all executed well.', '2008-04-23 18:26:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656075, 669855, 37252, '<td valign="top">The sky surely is dramatic. I think the crop on the bottom was too tight is all.</td>', 'The sky surely is dramatic. I think the crop on the bottom was too tight is all.', '2008-04-23 18:27:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4656078, 669967, 61958, '<td valign="top">It take a few second to regiter the bee in the photo which liekly didn''t go well with those who vote faster. for my part I think the image is too busy and lack simplicity especially when inverting the image. I think this is probably a pretty decent positive image though.</td>', 'It take a few second to regiter the bee in the photo which liekly didn''t go well with those who vote faster. for my part I think the image is too busy and lack simplicity especially when inverting the image. I think this is probably a pretty decent positive image though.', '2008-04-23 18:31:43.000000', NULL, 0),
