(4684214, 669750, 23098, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bvy:</b></div><hr/><i> No comments? I like this -- especially the clean lines and geometry of the building, and the chocolate tones. Maybe more contrast in the sky would have helped, but what do I know about negative? I did <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=668193" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">abysmally</a> in this challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, bvy.  This challenge was an interesting experience.   I agree with you about the sky - some contrast would have helped.   I was wishing there had been a cloud or two in the shot.  :)</td>', 'Originally posted by bvy: No comments? I like this -- especially the clean lines and geometry of the building, and the chocolate tones. Maybe more contrast in the sky would have helped, but what do I know about negative? I did abysmally in this challenge.   Thanks, bvy.  This challenge was an interesting experience.   I agree with you about the sky - some contrast would have helped.   I was wishing there had been a cloud or two in the shot.  :)', '2008-05-06 11:32:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4684219, 668193, 23098, '<td valign="top">Nice abstract.  The cold blue and icy sharp look of the tree trunk is what makes this one for me. <br/>I agree with bobonacus - too many ones. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-05-06 10:43:24.</i></td>', 'Nice abstract.  The cold blue and icy sharp look of the tree trunk is what makes this one for me. I agree with bobonacus - too many ones. ', '2008-05-06 11:41:53.000000', '2008-05-06 11:43:24.000000', 0),
(4684463, 669346, 76335, '<td valign="top">What a tough challenge this was. I like this, but I think the oversaturation might have hurt you. It is a little harsh. The other problem (out of your control) is the Basic editing parameters. There''s a lot of detail in this image that either got lost in the JPEG comression or the 640 size limit. I suspect it looked much better before resizing/compressing. Also, I''m very careful with USM after resize. It''s powerful, and these days, I''m actually finding more and more use for high pass sharpen. <br/> <br/>All that said, you did better in this challenge than I did! (which doesn''t say much).</td>', 'What a tough challenge this was. I like this, but I think the oversaturation might have hurt you. It is a little harsh. The other problem (out of your control) is the Basic editing parameters. There''s a lot of detail in this image that either got lost in the JPEG comression or the 640 size limit. I suspect it looked much better before resizing/compressing. Also, I''m very careful with USM after resize. It''s powerful, and these days, I''m actually finding more and more use for high pass sharpen.  All that said, you did better in this challenge than I did! (which doesn''t say much).', '2008-05-06 13:11:13.000000', NULL, 0),
